[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi everyone,</p>\n<p>I have been playing a bit with the <code>Task</code>construct and the (naive) associated parallel map:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">parMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tasks</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Task</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">spawn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">tasks</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">task</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">task</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Then I realized that given that each call to <code>Task.get</code>may lead to the creation of a new thread (to avoid deadlock by threadpool starvation) a lot of use cases would probably create many more threads than LEAN_NUM_THREADS and would collapse the performance of parMap.</p>\n<p>After reading about <code>Task.bind</code>, I came up with an alternate parallel map implementation:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getAllTask</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tasks</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Task</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">results</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[])</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Task</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tasks</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">results</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">reverse</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">task</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tasks</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">task</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">getAllTask</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tasks</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">results</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">parMap'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tasks</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Task</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">spawn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">getAllTask</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tasks</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But I have not found so far any example where <code>parMap'</code> is effectively  faster than <code>parMap</code> and I am not sure why (the synchronisation overhead ?).</p>\n<p>So I guess that my questions are</p>\n<p>- Is the overall approach sound? Are the specifics of <code>parMap'</code> correct?<br>\n  - What would be the \"right\" parallel map implementation if <code>parMap'</code> is not adequate?<br>\n  - Any concrete example where the the \"right\" parallel map beats the naive one?</p>\n<p>Best,</p>\n<p>Sébastien</p>",
        "id": 615903159,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Boisgérault",
        "timestamp": 1786467684
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>A litle correction, Task.get don't spawn a thread. Lean has a Thread Pool and a queue of Tasks that are dispatched to the the existing Thread Pool. <br>\nWhen you call Task.get, the current thread waits for the task to complete.<br>\nIf you want you can use <code>Task.mapList</code>, but not sure it will be faster than the naive one</p>",
        "id": 615917995,
        "sender_full_name": "Alfredo Moreira-Rosa",
        "timestamp": 1786471881
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>an example to check the speed :</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sequentialMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">parMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tasks</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Task</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">spawn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">tasks</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Task</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">parMap'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Task</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mapList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Task</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">spawn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expensive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">loop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">acc</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">loop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1000003</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">loop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10000</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">range</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1000</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">time</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- time: 3116ms</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sequentialMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expensive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">time</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- time: 508ms</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">parMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expensive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">time</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- time: 558ms</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">parMap'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expensive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 615918157,
        "sender_full_name": "Alfredo Moreira-Rosa",
        "timestamp": 1786471939
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"942100\">@Alfredo Moreira-Rosa</span>,</p>\n<p>Thank you for your reply!</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A litle correction, Task.get don't spawn a thread. Lean has a Thread Pool and a queue of Tasks that are dispatched to the the existing Thread Pool.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Agreed, It doesn't spawn a thread <em>directly</em>, but it temporarily increase the threadpool size by one, and therefore an existing task that was waiting can be started in a new thread. Right? (this is my understanding of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Init/Core.html#Task.get\">https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Init/Core.html#Task.get</a>)</p>\n<p>I didn't know about <code>Task.mapList</code>, thank you <span aria-label=\"pray\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f64f\" role=\"img\" title=\"pray\">:pray:</span>. Afaict with the default options, this is roughly my <code>parMap'</code> (<code>get</code>is not used and no thread is created in excess of <code>LEAN_NUM_THREADS</code>)</p>\n<p>Your experiments seem to reproduce what I was experiencing: the \"right\" way (<code>Task.mapList</code>, that binds and doesn't grow the threadpool) seems to perform about the same or slightly worse than the naive way (<code>get</code>each task), despite the large number of threads that could be created in the process. I was expecting (naively?) it to be much faster ...</p>\n<p>PS2. I didn't know about <code>#time</code> either, that's handy (I used the <code>timeit</code> function), thanks!</p>",
        "id": 615924034,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Boisgérault",
        "timestamp": 1786473801
    },
    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p>Agreed, It doesn't spawn a thread <em>directly</em>, but it temporarily increase the threadpool size by one, and therefore an existing task that was waiting can be started in a new thread. Right?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Yes, only if you are running parMap in a Task itself. in this case it's better indeed to use <code>mapList</code>.</p>",
        "id": 615927329,
        "sender_full_name": "Alfredo Moreira-Rosa",
        "timestamp": 1786474754
    },
    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p>Yes, only if you are running parMap in a Task itself.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This is one of the bits I don't get. Could you elaborate or give me some pointers?</p>",
        "id": 615934037,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Boisgérault",
        "timestamp": 1786476818
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's in the docs :</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If the current thread is itself executing a (non-dedicated) task, the maximum threadpool size is temporarily increased by one while waiting so as to ensure the process cannot be deadlocked by threadpool starvation</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Imagine you have all your threads in the thread pool busy waiting on another <code>Task</code> with <code>Task.get</code>. <br>\nIf the Threadpool did not augment it's number of threads you could deadlock the thread pool  because you are yourself being executed in threadpool with no hope to get your task scheduled, and have <code>Task.get</code> block forever.<br>\nThis cannot happen in the main thread. Indeed the main thread is not consuming any capacity on the Thread Pool (since it's not part of it), and then cannot starve it.</p>",
        "id": 615947206,
        "sender_full_name": "Alfredo Moreira-Rosa",
        "timestamp": 1786480851
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>OK, I see, thanks!</p>\n<p>(I had no intention to spawn dedicated tasks to begin with, so I never considered the \"dedicated\" case of the doc sentence, not realising that the clause also applied to the main thread.)  </p>\n<p>So the experiments with the naive parMap in the main thread actually never a chance to create too many threads, right? And actually, even if parMap uses many gets, the (potential) increase of the threadpool size is gone by the time the next get is reached, right? So even in this case, we probably cannot decrease the performance significantly be creating too many threads and the naive parMap is actually not that bad?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">time</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- time: 503ms</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">parMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expensive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">time</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- time: 509ms</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Task</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">spawn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">parMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expensive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Complete code in Lean live: <a href=\"https://live.lean-lang.org/#codez=CYUwZgBADghgTgWRlCBvQjcAUE3ABfCAKSALgk0CTCbASgIA8BnCEgGQEs6AXU65tzrRgLwAoCBAA2ITuxh0A1gyICI9AHQBbZBDABXAHbKIAgHwjREACozZKurADu%2BwnogB9Q0a3LKp6XLrrNSzkVAHNJISFQSBAaKBBdOhYANxACfRIAORh2bggszkVTCU44EABjcQB7SpR8FggYMorM7O5hMwgWSHqlAAYIdgALeNMOxrLRiBAxOhBJ0TFq2vqAWggARmp8cYgAagJ6gCpO6gBSDd7Ly4BmbyKli5criF0IqM7dKG0CiFYOPOygl%2BvBUcBgujCGyelwiAGJ2Cw1KkVmsEUiSABWXrXNR0ISwkBJGBiaDwJAoGJxBLJVIsT7fCAAHyMKgkEKGcLRyNRiJAmN6AE5cfjCcSCEFrLYYA4tM43MYCLBEJpKfFEikPl8cpRQpImSy2SEOUIgA\">https://live.lean-lang.org/#codez=CYUwZgBADghgTgWRlCBvQjcAUE3ABfCAKSALgk0CTCbASgIA8BnCEgGQEs6AXU65tzrRgLwAoCBAA2ITuxh0A1gyICI9AHQBbZBDABXAHbKIAgHwjREACozZKurADu%2BwnogB9Q0a3LKp6XLrrNSzkVAHNJISFQSBAaKBBdOhYANxACfRIAORh2bggszkVTCU44EABjcQB7SpR8FggYMorM7O5hMwgWSHqlAAYIdgALeNMOxrLRiBAxOhBJ0TFq2vqAWggARmp8cYgAagJ6gCpO6gBSDd7Ly4BmbyKli5criF0IqM7dKG0CiFYOPOygl%2BvBUcBgujCGyelwiAGJ2Cw1KkVmsEUiSABWXrXNR0ISwkBJGBiaDwJAoGJxBLJVIsT7fCAAHyMKgkEKGcLRyNRiJAmN6AE5cfjCcSCEFrLYYA4tM43MYCLBEJpKfFEikPl8cpRQpImSy2SEOUIgA</a></p>",
